---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[\"backup\"])"
---
Save every readable setting to one JSON file. Needs web-config; in a gamepad mode the control channel takes the pad there and back. With control channel v1.6, the file also has the saved config as one blob, for `restore`

Usage: gamepadii backup [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` and `leds` only
          
          [default: human]

  -o, --output <FILE>
          Where to write it [default: ~/.local/share/gamepadii/backups/<time>-<board>.json]

      --channel-only
          Save only the config blob, over the control channel (v1.6), in any mode: no web-config, no restart

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --stay
          Leave the pad in web-config afterwards instead of rebooting it back into its gamepad mode

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

      --timeout <SECS>
          How long to wait for the pad on USB after each reboot
          
          [default: 10]

      --no-channel
          Don't use the USB control channel (the gamepadii firmware's): only web-config and button presses

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
